>hard, so I think that on balance it's worth it.)

I usually stick to all gems I find. After a while, you will have a lot
of different types of gems, and of each color there is ONE type that
you have quite a lot of. This is almost certainly the worthless piece
of glass you're looking for. Don't identify these, but throw them at
unicorns. Unidentified gems will add one to your luck (identified real
ones add 5, but you lose a real gem). Don't (N)ame the gems, though,
because an unidentified, named gem will NOT add to your luck when
thrown at a unicorn.

